WEBVTT

00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:06.400
It was a small pain we felt.

00:00:07.890 --> 00:00:12.360
Our feelings, which should have reached
them, were stopped in their tracks.

00:00:13.770 --> 00:00:17.870
Our wishes and hearts have been entangled,
and our hopes intertwined.

00:00:18.550 --> 00:00:20.500
We seemed to be losing sight of the truth...

00:00:21.580 --> 00:00:23.500
Even if they have a sorrowful past...

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:26.170
Even if their future is dark and hazy...

00:00:26.170 --> 00:00:28.290
we still have to face them.

00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:33.130
Everyone is surely fighting
for the same future.

00:00:35.180 --> 00:00:39.050
Mahou Shoujo Lyrical
Nanoha A's will now begin.

00:02:39.340 --> 00:02:43.180
Fate-san has taken some critical
damage to her Linker Core, but...

00:02:43.600 --> 00:02:45.810
it seems her life isn't in danger.

00:02:45.810 --> 00:02:50.810
It was mostly sucked up by the Book of
Darkness, just like what happened to me.

00:02:50.810 --> 00:02:52.810
It's a good thing we were working
aboard the Arthra at the time.

00:02:52.810 --> 00:02:56.440
We were able to get to her faster
than when it happened to Nanoha.

00:02:56.440 --> 00:02:57.570
Yeah.

00:02:58.150 --> 00:03:02.240
Shortly after you two were sent out,
the station's control system was cracked,

00:03:02.240 --> 00:03:04.580
issued an error, and then shut down.

00:03:04.580 --> 00:03:08.080
Because of that, I couldn't issue
commands or contact anyone else...

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:11.370
I'm sorry. I'm responsible
for what happened.

00:03:13.330 --> 00:03:14.880
No, you're not.

00:03:14.880 --> 00:03:17.710
Because you quickly got
the system back online,

00:03:17.710 --> 00:03:20.550
you were able to get in touch
with the Arthra afterwards.

00:03:20.550 --> 00:03:23.390
And you were also able to capture
an image of that masked guy.

00:03:24.220 --> 00:03:25.970
But this is strange...

00:03:25.970 --> 00:03:30.890
The equipment we use down there
runs on the same system as up here.

00:03:30.890 --> 00:03:34.810
Is there really someone out there who
could crack it from an external point?

00:03:34.810 --> 00:03:36.480
Yes, you're right!

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:41.990
They went through the firewall and alert
system, and forced the whole system down.

00:03:41.990 --> 00:03:44.780
It's a little hard to believe.

00:03:44.780 --> 00:03:49.500
I've shifted the units around, but we need
to come up with a stronger security system.

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:53.460
Does that mean someone with incredible
technological skills is out there?

00:03:53.460 --> 00:03:57.710
Yeah. They might even be
working for an organization.

00:03:57.710 --> 00:03:59.960
From what you've said,

00:03:59.960 --> 00:04:02.880
the conditions, and how they interact
with each other, are still unclear.

00:04:02.880 --> 00:04:03.840
Yeah...

00:04:03.840 --> 00:04:08.680
By the time I learned what happened,
the masked man had already left.

00:04:08.680 --> 00:04:13.690
But she was...
Signum was holding Fate...

00:04:13.690 --> 00:04:18.480
and she said, "I have no excuse
to give you, but I'm sorry."

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:21.990
Alex! The Arthra's flight
controls are good to go, right?

00:04:21.990 --> 00:04:22.990
Correct.

00:04:22.990 --> 00:04:25.990
Good. Even though it's a
bit earlier than planned,

00:04:25.990 --> 00:04:28.240
we will move headquarters
back to the Arthra.

00:04:28.240 --> 00:04:30.290
All staff are to return to normal stations.

00:04:30.290 --> 00:04:30.910
Yes, ma'am.

00:04:30.910 --> 00:04:34.210
And we'll have to send
you home, Nanoha-san.

00:04:34.210 --> 00:04:35.920
Ah... yes. But...

00:04:35.920 --> 00:04:38.840
If you're worried about Fate-san, don't be.

00:04:38.840 --> 00:04:40.800
After all, we'll be here
to keep an eye on her.

00:04:43.300 --> 00:04:44.470
Okay.

00:04:45.550 --> 00:04:48.850
A Sad Resolve, and a Courageous Choice.

00:04:53.980 --> 00:04:57.480
Since he saved us, that means
he's on our side, right...?

00:04:57.480 --> 00:05:02.360
At the very least, it's obvious he wants
to see the Book of Darkness completed.

00:05:02.360 --> 00:05:07.160
He might be planning to use it for his own
purposes after it's completed...

00:05:07.160 --> 00:05:08.240
That's not possible!

00:05:08.240 --> 00:05:13.500
Even if he stole it once it was completed,
only its master can use it!

00:05:13.500 --> 00:05:18.040
Once its complete, our master
will gain absolute power.

00:05:18.040 --> 00:05:21.500
It shouldn't be possible to threaten or
brainwash her once that's happened.

00:05:21.500 --> 00:05:25.720
At any rate, I've set up a strong
security field around the house,

00:05:25.720 --> 00:05:30.470
so I doubt there's any chance
of Hayate-chan being harmed.

00:05:30.470 --> 00:05:35.230
But just in case, you should try to stay
by our master's side from now on.

00:05:35.230 --> 00:05:36.480
Yeah.

00:05:36.480 --> 00:05:41.770
Hey, once we complete the Book of Darkness
and Hayate becomes its true master,

00:05:41.770 --> 00:05:45.070
she'll be happy, right?

00:05:45.570 --> 00:05:46.820
What's all this now?

00:05:46.820 --> 00:05:49.990
The master of the Book of Darkness
gains incredible power.

00:05:49.990 --> 00:05:53.700
As its guardians, we know that best.

00:05:54.370 --> 00:05:55.750
True...

00:05:55.750 --> 00:05:57.420
True, but...

00:05:57.420 --> 00:06:02.040
I feel like we're forgetting
something really important...

00:06:41.330 --> 00:06:42.380
Hayate!

00:06:42.380 --> 00:06:43.630
Hayate-chan!

00:06:44.340 --> 00:06:47.090
Hayate! Hayate!

00:06:48.300 --> 00:06:50.430
Get her to the hospital!
Call an ambulance!

00:06:50.430 --> 00:06:50.890
Yeah.

00:06:50.890 --> 00:06:52.600
Don't move her!
Leave her right where she is!

00:06:52.600 --> 00:06:53.390
Y-Yeah.

00:07:02.360 --> 00:07:04.860
Fate-san. You're finally awake.

00:07:04.860 --> 00:07:06.860
Admiral Lindy...?

00:07:06.860 --> 00:07:07.530
Yeah.

00:07:15.030 --> 00:07:15.870
Arf...

00:07:15.870 --> 00:07:19.750
Arf's been watching
over you since last night.

00:07:20.710 --> 00:07:22.710
Huh? Where am–

00:07:22.710 --> 00:07:24.750
You're aboard the Arthra.

00:07:24.750 --> 00:07:29.260
In your battle on the desert planet, you were
attacked from behind and lost consciousness.

00:07:30.380 --> 00:07:34.680
Your Linker Core was absorbed, but the
doctors say you'll be better in no time.

00:07:34.680 --> 00:07:35.390
Don't worry.

00:07:35.390 --> 00:07:38.390
So... they got me, huh?

00:07:38.390 --> 00:07:41.890
Not even the Administrative Bureau's
scanners could catch the attack.

00:07:41.890 --> 00:07:43.020
There was no way to avoid it.

00:07:45.900 --> 00:07:48.650
Ah, I'm sorry.
Did you not like that?

00:07:48.650 --> 00:07:51.650
No... I did, but...

00:07:51.650 --> 00:07:54.700
It looked like you were
having a bad dream...

00:07:54.700 --> 00:07:57.160
But I'm glad you're all right.

00:07:57.160 --> 00:08:00.910
I'm sorry... and thank you very much.

00:08:00.910 --> 00:08:05.630
I told the school that you'll be missing a few
days due to some things going on at home.

00:08:05.630 --> 00:08:07.460
You should take this time to rest.

00:08:07.460 --> 00:08:08.090
Okay.

00:08:08.090 --> 00:08:09.630
You're hungry, right?

00:08:10.920 --> 00:08:14.220
I'll bring you something
light to eat and drink.

00:08:14.220 --> 00:08:15.260
What would you like?

00:08:15.260 --> 00:08:17.390
You don't have to–

00:08:17.390 --> 00:08:18.850
It's fine.

00:08:18.850 --> 00:08:21.980
Umm... I'll let you decide, then.

00:08:21.980 --> 00:08:23.190
Alright.

00:08:33.570 --> 00:08:34.950
Fate...

00:08:39.580 --> 00:08:42.580
Yes, it looks like you're all right.
Thank goodness.

00:08:42.580 --> 00:08:45.080
Yes. Thank you very much.

00:08:45.080 --> 00:08:47.460
I'm relieved.

00:08:47.460 --> 00:08:52.470
I told you. I just felt a little dizzy,
and my hand cramped up on my chest.

00:08:52.470 --> 00:08:55.510
Really, they're always making
something out of nothing.

00:08:55.510 --> 00:08:59.010
But you did hit your head...

00:08:59.010 --> 00:09:01.060
And it'd be bad if something
happened to you.

00:09:01.060 --> 00:09:03.430
Hayate! Thank goodness.

00:09:03.430 --> 00:09:05.350
Since you guys are all here anyway,

00:09:05.350 --> 00:09:08.900
I'd like to do some examinations,
so just sit tight a little longer, okay?

00:09:08.900 --> 00:09:10.480
Alright.

00:09:10.480 --> 00:09:13.740
Now then, Signum-san, Shamal-san,
could I speak to you for a minute?

00:09:13.740 --> 00:09:14.780
Yes?

00:09:18.990 --> 00:09:22.620
Nothing new showed up
in today's examinations, but...

00:09:22.620 --> 00:09:26.080
I don't think her hand just
"cramped up" like that.

00:09:26.080 --> 00:09:29.250
Yes... she looked like
she was in a lot of pain.

00:09:29.250 --> 00:09:32.710
This might be a sign of
the paralysis spreading.

00:09:32.710 --> 00:09:35.720
She didn't have symptoms
like this in the past, right?

00:09:35.720 --> 00:09:42.310
I don't think so, but...
Hayate-chan hides her pain from us.

00:09:42.310 --> 00:09:44.810
There's no guarantee that she
won't have another seizure.

00:09:44.810 --> 00:09:48.690
To be on the safe side, I think we should
keep her hospitalized for a while.

00:09:49.440 --> 00:09:50.820
Would that be all right?

00:09:53.400 --> 00:09:54.190
Yes.

00:09:56.110 --> 00:09:57.400
Hospitalization?

00:09:57.400 --> 00:09:59.740
Yes... that's what she said...

00:10:02.410 --> 00:10:05.960
But it's only for some examinations
and just in case something goes wrong.

00:10:05.960 --> 00:10:07.670
There's nothing to worry about.

00:10:07.670 --> 00:10:08.420
Right?

00:10:08.420 --> 00:10:09.170
That's right.

00:10:10.630 --> 00:10:13.590
That's fine, but...

00:10:13.590 --> 00:10:17.130
if I'm hospitalized here,
who will make your meals?

00:10:18.260 --> 00:10:21.680
W-We'll do something about that.

00:10:22.350 --> 00:10:25.180
Yeah. We'll be fine... probably.

00:10:26.680 --> 00:10:29.650
We'll come to see you every day!
So... don't worry.

00:10:31.310 --> 00:10:33.150
Vita, you're such a good girl.

00:10:33.150 --> 00:10:35.570
But it doesn't have to be every day.

00:10:35.570 --> 00:10:38.360
There's nothing to do here,
so you'd be really bored, Vita.

00:10:38.360 --> 00:10:39.570
Y-Yeah...

00:10:42.620 --> 00:10:47.330
I'll probably just take it easy and
get lots of sleep while I'm here.

00:10:49.460 --> 00:10:53.250
Oh, no! Suzuka-chan might text me.

00:10:53.250 --> 00:10:56.130
Ah, I'll contact her for you.

00:10:56.130 --> 00:10:58.090
Please do.

00:10:58.970 --> 00:11:02.220
Well, we'll go home and get
a change of clothes for you.

00:11:02.220 --> 00:11:03.800
Let us know if you need anything else.

00:11:04.310 --> 00:11:07.310
What else would be good...?

00:11:20.570 --> 00:11:21.780
Vita.

00:11:22.570 --> 00:11:23.570
Y-Yeah.

00:12:15.290 --> 00:12:19.250
<i>Okay. I'll report what
I've learned so far.</i>

00:12:20.170 --> 00:12:23.760
<i>To begin with, the "Book of Darkness"
isn't its true name.</i>

00:12:24.510 --> 00:12:29.060
<i>According to ancient sources, its official
name is the "Tome of the Night Sky."</i>

00:12:29.720 --> 00:12:34.270
<i>It was originally made to gather spells
from great mages all around the universe</i>

00:12:34.270 --> 00:12:38.480
<i>and study them,
traveling together with its master.</i>

00:12:39.480 --> 00:12:41.860
<i>I think it started to be used for destruction</i>

00:12:41.860 --> 00:12:43.820
<i>because someone in the
later generations of masters</i>

00:12:43.820 --> 00:12:46.910
<i>probably altered its original program.</i>

00:12:46.910 --> 00:12:53.080
<i>I guess that means that in the past,
just like now, there we fools</i>

00:12:53.080 --> 00:12:55.620
<i>who recklessly tried to gain the
enormous powers of a Lost Logia.</i>

00:12:56.170 --> 00:12:57.960
<i>Because of that alteration,</i>

00:12:57.960 --> 00:13:04.050
<i>its traveling and automatic data restoration
functions have gone out of control.</i>

00:13:04.050 --> 00:13:07.550
And that's why it can reappear anywhere,
reincarnating eternally?

00:13:07.550 --> 00:13:10.060
If it's ancient magic we're talking about,
I'd say that's a good possibility.

00:13:10.060 --> 00:13:14.310
<i>Its cruelest feature is the
effect it has on its master.</i>

00:13:15.100 --> 00:13:16.940
<i>If it doesn't collect anything over a fixed period of time,</i>

00:13:16.940 --> 00:13:20.320
<i>it starts eating into its own master's magical capacity.</i>

00:13:21.820 --> 00:13:25.820
<i>Furthermore, once it's completed, it uses
its master's magical power without limits...</i>

00:13:25.820 --> 00:13:27.320
<i>for indiscriminate destruction.</i>

00:13:28.370 --> 00:13:32.580
<i>Which is why, soon after completion,
all of its masters thus far have...</i>

00:13:32.580 --> 00:13:37.370
Right... how about any documents
regarding stopping or sealing it?

00:13:37.370 --> 00:13:39.590
<i>I'm investigating that right now,</i>

00:13:39.590 --> 00:13:42.710
<i>but stopping it before it's complete
will probably be difficult...</i>

00:13:42.710 --> 00:13:43.380
Why?

00:13:43.840 --> 00:13:47.050
<i>If the true master of the Book of Darkness
hasn't been recognized and accepted,</i>

00:13:47.050 --> 00:13:50.180
<i>they won't be able to use their
administrative powers over the system.</i>

00:13:50.180 --> 00:13:53.720
<i>In other words, stopping or altering the
program is impossible until that's happened.</i>

00:13:55.890 --> 00:13:58.730
<i>If you try to forcefully operate
it from an external point,</i>

00:13:58.730 --> 00:14:02.400
<i>it has a system that will absorb its master
completely and reincarnate again elsewhere.</i>

00:14:02.400 --> 00:14:09.110
<i>Yeah... that's why it's said that permanently
sealing the Book of Darkness is impossible.</i>

00:14:09.110 --> 00:14:13.660
What was previously a repository
of magic has turned into this...

00:14:14.750 --> 00:14:18.830
I almost feel sorry for the Book of Darkness...
or rather, the Tome of the Night Sky.

00:14:19.370 --> 00:14:20.920
Is that all you've learned so far?

00:14:20.920 --> 00:14:22.090
<i>At this time, yes.</i>

00:14:22.920 --> 00:14:24.590
<i>But I'm still investigating.</i>

00:14:24.590 --> 00:14:27.130
<i>Though really, I should have expected
this from the Infinity Library.</i>

00:14:27.130 --> 00:14:29.380
<i>It's amazing... anything I
search for appears in here.</i>

00:14:30.180 --> 00:14:33.100
<i>From my point of view,
you're the amazing one.</i>

00:14:33.100 --> 00:14:35.180
<i>You have one heck of an ability
for investigating things.</i>

00:14:35.180 --> 00:14:37.680
I'm sorry, but please continue
for a little while longer.

00:14:37.680 --> 00:14:38.730
<i>Got it.</i>

00:14:38.730 --> 00:14:39.770
<i>Aria, you too.</i>

00:14:39.770 --> 00:14:42.650
<i>Yep. Lotte, switch with me later, okay?</i>

00:14:42.650 --> 00:14:43.940
Okay, Aria!

00:14:43.940 --> 00:14:45.190
Do your best!

00:14:46.190 --> 00:14:48.200
Yuuno-kun really is something else.

00:14:48.200 --> 00:14:51.570
Yeah. Honestly,
I'm really surprised, too.

00:14:51.570 --> 00:14:52.240
Yeah.

00:14:52.780 --> 00:14:53.450
Amy...

00:14:53.950 --> 00:14:56.250
put a picture of the
masked man on the screen.

00:14:56.250 --> 00:14:57.000
Sure thing.

00:14:57.500 --> 00:14:59.210
Have an idea about him?

00:14:59.210 --> 00:15:00.000
More or less.

00:15:01.330 --> 00:15:06.760
This guy's abilities are more than amazing...
They're more like "impossible."

00:15:06.760 --> 00:15:09.010
If you were to teleport from one
of these two worlds to the other,

00:15:09.010 --> 00:15:12.760
it would take twenty minutes
at the fastest speed possible.

00:15:12.760 --> 00:15:16.270
But to defend against a direct hit
from Nanoha-chan's new Buster,

00:15:16.270 --> 00:15:18.770
quickly release a long-distance bind,

00:15:19.480 --> 00:15:21.730
and then in only nine minutes

00:15:21.730 --> 00:15:25.770
sneak up behind Fate-chan without being
noticed and attack with such power...

00:15:25.770 --> 00:15:28.740
He must be some kind of veteran at this...

00:15:28.740 --> 00:15:31.530
Yeah. Even I can't do that.

00:15:31.530 --> 00:15:32.780
How about you, Lotte?

00:15:34.320 --> 00:15:38.040
Totally impossible, I'm no good
at long-distance magic as it is.

00:15:38.500 --> 00:15:42.250
Aria's the magic instructor and
you're the physical instructor,

00:15:42.250 --> 00:15:44.540
so both roles are split
between you evenly, right?

00:15:44.540 --> 00:15:46.210
Right, right!

00:15:46.920 --> 00:15:50.170
And because of that, I sure went
through a lot in the past...

00:15:50.170 --> 00:15:52.260
But you became stronger
because of it, right?

00:15:52.260 --> 00:15:53.800
Be grateful!

00:16:04.810 --> 00:16:06.690
<i>Are you feeling all right?</i>

00:16:06.690 --> 00:16:11.860
<i>Yeah. I'm a little uneasy without my magic,
but my body's back to normal.</i>

00:16:12.820 --> 00:16:18.620
<i>They said we're to quietly live normal
lives here until we're called back.</i>

00:16:18.620 --> 00:16:21.830
<i>So it's like... we're on standby?</i>

00:16:21.830 --> 00:16:24.790
<i>Yeah. It looks like they're increasing
the number of armed Bureau members</i>

00:16:24.790 --> 00:16:26.840
<i>and refocusing on the pursuit
part of the investigation.</i>

00:16:27.340 --> 00:16:28.630
<i>I see.</i>

00:16:33.430 --> 00:16:34.430
Hospitalized?

00:16:34.430 --> 00:16:36.390
Hayate-chan was?

00:16:36.390 --> 00:16:37.220
Yeah.

00:16:37.800 --> 00:16:40.390
I got a message last night saying so.

00:16:40.390 --> 00:16:43.100
She looked fine the last time I saw her,

00:16:43.100 --> 00:16:45.940
but there are a lot of medical tests they
have to perform, and that'll take a while.

00:16:47.650 --> 00:16:48.860
I see...

00:16:49.610 --> 00:16:53.070
Then, do you wanna go visit her after school?

00:16:53.860 --> 00:16:54.910
Really?

00:16:54.910 --> 00:16:57.240
She's your friend, right?

00:16:57.240 --> 00:16:59.990
And you did say you'd introduce us.

00:16:59.990 --> 00:17:03.210
And since we're going to visit her in the
hospital, the more the merrier, right?

00:17:03.210 --> 00:17:06.790
Yeah... I'm not too sure
about barging in like that...

00:17:06.790 --> 00:17:09.090
But I think it'd be all right.

00:17:09.090 --> 00:17:09.800
Right?

00:17:09.800 --> 00:17:11.880
Thanks!

00:17:15.680 --> 00:17:16.640
Here we go.

00:17:24.850 --> 00:17:26.650
It's from Suzuka-chan.

00:17:27.400 --> 00:17:29.310
"Dear Shamal-san,"

00:17:29.310 --> 00:17:32.150
"Hello. Tsukimura Suzuka here."

00:17:32.150 --> 00:17:36.780
"I'd like to go visit Hayate-chan in the
hospital with my friends after school today."

00:17:36.780 --> 00:17:38.950
"Would that be all right?"

00:17:38.950 --> 00:17:41.240
Suzuka-chan... you're such a good girl.

00:17:48.420 --> 00:17:50.840
"If it's not a good time, or there's a problem,

00:17:50.840 --> 00:17:54.760
could you at least show
this picture to her, please?"

00:18:04.180 --> 00:18:05.520
<i>What?!</i>

00:18:07.190 --> 00:18:09.020
What did you say Testarossa
and the others are doing?

00:18:09.020 --> 00:18:12.730
Like I've been saying,
Testarossa-chan and Nanoha-chan,

00:18:12.730 --> 00:18:17.150
the two mages from the Administrative
Bureau, are going to see Hayate-chan today!

00:18:17.150 --> 00:18:19.030
Because they're Suzuka-chan's friends!

00:18:19.660 --> 00:18:20.660
What do we do? What do we do?!

00:18:20.660 --> 00:18:23.080
Hold on. Calm down, Shamal. It's fine.

00:18:23.080 --> 00:18:25.700
Thankfully, most of Master
Hayate's magical potential

00:18:25.700 --> 00:18:27.500
is held within the Book of Darkness.

00:18:27.500 --> 00:18:29.830
Unless they perform a very deep scan,
she won't be found out.

00:18:29.830 --> 00:18:32.840
Y-You may be right, but...

00:18:32.840 --> 00:18:36.630
In other words, as long as they don't
run into us there, it should be fine.

00:18:37.760 --> 00:18:40.840
It was a mistake showing our faces...

00:18:40.840 --> 00:18:44.390
I should've used some transformation magic
on us the last time we were attacked...

00:18:44.850 --> 00:18:47.020
No use regretting that now.

00:18:47.020 --> 00:18:50.230
When her friends are visiting,
we should withdraw.

00:18:50.230 --> 00:18:51.060
Yeah.

00:18:51.480 --> 00:18:57.570
All that's left is to ask Master Hayate
and Dr. Ishida to not say our names.

00:18:57.570 --> 00:19:01.280
I hope Hayate-chan won't
think that's weird...

00:19:01.280 --> 00:19:03.830
We have no choice.
I'm counting on you.

00:19:03.830 --> 00:19:04.580
Yeah.

00:19:06.330 --> 00:19:07.580
Yes?

00:19:07.580 --> 00:19:09.000
Please come in.

00:19:10.670 --> 00:19:12.080
Hello!

00:19:16.090 --> 00:19:18.720
Hello! Welcome!

00:19:18.720 --> 00:19:20.220
Sorry for intruding.

00:19:20.220 --> 00:19:21.970
Hayate-chan, are you all right?

00:19:21.970 --> 00:19:23.800
Yeah, I'm fine.

00:19:24.640 --> 00:19:26.220
Everyone, have a seat.

00:19:26.220 --> 00:19:27.890
Thanks.

00:19:27.890 --> 00:19:29.730
The coat rack's over there, too.

00:19:29.730 --> 00:19:30.480
Okay.

00:19:30.940 --> 00:19:33.730
This cake was made at
my family's coffee shop.

00:19:33.730 --> 00:19:35.020
Really?

00:19:35.020 --> 00:19:36.110
It's really good!

00:19:36.110 --> 00:19:37.110
I'm so happy!

00:19:38.190 --> 00:19:41.030
Shamal-san?
What are you doing?

00:19:41.030 --> 00:19:44.910
I... I was just wondering
who came over, so...

00:19:44.910 --> 00:19:47.910
Why don't you just go inside?

00:19:47.910 --> 00:19:49.910
Unless you're out here
for some other reason?

00:19:50.540 --> 00:19:52.920
Umm... well...

00:19:56.460 --> 00:19:59.170
This may sound a little strange,

00:19:59.170 --> 00:20:03.430
but as Hayate-chan's attending physician,
I'm really grateful to you all.

00:20:03.430 --> 00:20:08.430
Ever since you started living with her,
Hayate-chan's seemed so much happier.

00:20:10.390 --> 00:20:14.810
Honestly, Hayate-chan's
illness is a difficult one,

00:20:14.810 --> 00:20:17.020
but we're fighting it with
all the science we have.

00:20:17.020 --> 00:20:17.610
I see...

00:20:17.610 --> 00:20:21.240
Hayate-chan is the one
who's hurting the most.

00:20:21.240 --> 00:20:24.410
But with the support you and
her friends are giving her,

00:20:24.410 --> 00:20:26.620
I think she'll become much
more energetic and courageous.

00:20:27.120 --> 00:20:32.410
Please continue to support her,
so Hayate-chan can fight off this illness.

00:20:36.330 --> 00:20:37.340
We will...

00:20:43.510 --> 00:20:45.390
I hope she gets better soon.

00:20:45.390 --> 00:20:47.140
Yeah, me too.

00:20:49.060 --> 00:20:51.520
How was the visit with your friends?

00:20:51.520 --> 00:20:54.940
Everyone was really nice.
We had lots of fun.

00:20:54.940 --> 00:20:56.520
They said they'd come again
every now and then, too.

00:20:56.520 --> 00:20:58.690
That's great.

00:20:58.690 --> 00:21:01.740
But that aside,
it's almost Christmas, huh?

00:21:01.740 --> 00:21:04.450
This'll be my first Christmas with all of you,

00:21:04.450 --> 00:21:08.240
I hope I can get out of the hospital by then,
and we can have a great time together!

00:21:08.240 --> 00:21:11.240
Yes... it would be wonderful
if that could happen...

00:21:33.730 --> 00:21:38.730
<i>It looks like the Book of Darkness is
devouring Hayate-chan even faster now...</i>

00:21:39.480 --> 00:21:45.740
<i>At this rate, she only has another
month... or maybe even less.</i>

00:21:53.700 --> 00:21:55.910
<i>Something's strange...</i>

00:21:56.710 --> 00:21:59.750
<i>My memories are telling me
something's not right...</i>

00:22:01.590 --> 00:22:05.510
<i>But right now, this is all we can do.</i>

00:22:06.510 --> 00:22:12.100
I wouldn't be able to stand it if Hayate-chan
wasn't able to smile anymore... or if she dies!

00:22:12.100 --> 00:22:12.510
Yes.

00:22:19.230 --> 00:22:21.360
Let's do this, Eisen!

00:22:21.360 --> 00:22:22.860
Explosion.

00:22:26.490 --> 00:22:28.240
Gigant!

00:22:29.410 --> 00:22:31.530
Destroy it!

00:22:44.300 --> 00:22:45.590
Father,

00:22:46.300 --> 00:22:49.430
it's not healthy for you to work so hard.

00:22:49.430 --> 00:22:50.680
Yeah.

00:22:50.680 --> 00:22:51.850
Lieses, huh?

00:22:51.850 --> 00:22:53.180
How go things?

00:22:53.180 --> 00:22:55.220
Things are going nicely, little by little.

00:22:55.220 --> 00:22:57.430
Chrono and the others
are also doing their best,

00:22:57.430 --> 00:23:01.060
but they are facing the Book of Darkness,
so it won't be easy going.

00:23:01.060 --> 00:23:02.610
I see...

00:23:03.860 --> 00:23:08.190
I'm truly sorry about this...
having you two join me in this affair as well.

00:23:08.190 --> 00:23:10.160
What are you saying, Father?

00:23:10.160 --> 00:23:15.450
We're your familiars.
Your wish is our wish!

00:23:15.450 --> 00:23:18.120
Yeah. Everything will be fine, Father.

00:23:18.120 --> 00:23:20.580
Durandal's complete now, too.

00:23:20.580 --> 00:23:24.540
So the Book of Darkness's sealing will
definitely go all right this time!

00:23:24.540 --> 00:23:25.380
Yeah!

00:23:28.550 --> 00:23:29.550
Right...

00:25:09.270 --> 00:25:11.480
The Book of Darkness is
completed before our very eyes.

00:25:11.480 --> 00:25:13.740
But in exchange, <i>that</i> happened.

00:25:13.740 --> 00:25:19.870
Whether it was coincidence,
inevitable, or destiny...

00:25:19.870 --> 00:25:23.120
The time that had stopped
now begins to move.

00:25:23.120 --> 00:25:26.330
Next time on
Mahou Shoujo Lyrical Nanoha A's:

00:25:26.330 --> 00:25:27.750
Episode 9:

00:25:27.750 --> 00:25:29.210
Christmas Eve.

00:25:29.210 --> 00:25:32.050
Drive Ignition!
